  "updateinfo_id": "ALSA-2026:102648",
  "description": "SQLite is a C library that implements an SQL database engine. A large subset of SQL92 is supported. A complete database is stored in a single disk file. The API is designed for convenience and ease of use. Applications that link against SQLite can enjoy the power and flexibility of an SQL database without the administrative hassles of supporting a separate database server.  \n\nSecurity Fix(es):  \n\n  * sqlite: sqlite: Arbitrary command execution via .recover command (CVE-2026-119586)\n  * sqlite: sqlite: Denial of Service via stack exhaustion from chained COLLATE operators (CVE-2026-119376)\n  * sqlite: sqlite: Information disclosure via undersized WAL page size (CVE-2026-119375)\n  * sqlite: sqlite: Denial of service via heap-based buffer overflow in FTS5 (CVE-2026-119373)\n  * sqlite: sqlite: Denial of Service via use-after-free in R-Tree extension (CVE-2026-119378)\n  * sqlite: sqlite: Denial of Service via stack exhaustion from deeply nested Common Table Expressions (CVE-2026-119371)\n  * sqlite: sqlite: Denial of Service via use-after-free in full-text search (CVE-2026-119372)\n\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.\n",
  "fromstr": "packager@almalinux.org",
